Ba4 Nf6 9. Qf3 O-O 10. Bg5 d6 11. Nd2 h6 12. Bxf6 Qxf6 13. Qxf6 gxf6 14. Bb3
Bg4 {Aitken adds John Nunn offered the draw. This was the 3rd game on the same
day so both players were probably happy to go home. Aitken made a mess of the
score. This was very rare for him - tiredness? He missed out moves and got
some in the wrong order. The corrected score sheet strongly hints at a 62 year
old playing his third game of the day. (Geoff Chandler) Source: Aitken Book 32}
1/2-1/2

