1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. c5 Nd5 5. Bc4 e6 6. Nc3 Nxc3 7. dxc3 d5 ({
More usual is} 7... Nc6 8. Bf4 Bxc5 9. Qg4 {, etc.}) 8. cxd6 cxd6 9. Bf4 ({
The most accurate. Black can meet} 9. Nf3 {with} Qc7 {and his problems are
over.}) 9... Nc6 10. Nf3 d5 ({Objectively best is} 10... dxe5 {but after the
exchange of queens Black has no chances whatsoever of winning and would have
to play very accurately to hold the game.}) 11. Bd3 Bd7 12. O-O Rc8 13. Re1 Bc5
14. b4 Bb6 15. a4 a6 16. Qd2 Ne7 {One of Black's problems is that if he
castles he is very quickly mated.} 17. a5 Ba7 18. Rac1 Bb5 19. Bb1 Ng6 20. Be3
Bxe3 21. Qxe3 Qd7 22. Nd4 Ne7 23. f4 g6 {Black must try to stop f5 but with
his king stuck in the middle it is just not possible.} 24. g4 h5 25. f5 {
Of course! Now Black's weaknesses will be exposed.} hxg4 26. fxe6 fxe6 27. Qg5
Rg8 {Forced.} 28. Qxg4 Nf5 29. Bxf5 exf5 30. Qg3 {White must not allow ...
Bd3-e4.} Bc4 {To prevent the knight going to c5.} 31. e6 Qc7 ({Forced. If} 
31... Qe7 32. Nxf5) ({or} 31... Qh7 32. e7 Rg7 33. Re6 Rxe7 34. Rce1 {and it's
all over.}) 32. Qf3 Rh8 33. Qg2 Qh7 {We were both in some time trouble here so
I put out some bait...} 34. Re3 f4 {And he takes it! Now it's all over.} 35.
Rh3 Qxh3 36. Qxg6+ Kd8 37. Qf6+ Kc7 38. Qe5+ (38. Qe5+ {He sees that he will
be mated;} Kd8 39. Qd6+ Ke8 40. Qd7+ Kf8 41. Qf7#) 1-0

