1. c4 g6 2. g3 Bg7 3. Bg2 e5 4. Nc3 d6 5. e3 Nc6 6. Nge2 Nh6 7. O-O O-O 8. Rb1
Bf5 9. d3 Qd7 10. Nd5 Bh3 11. e4 ({Not} 11. Bxh3 Qxh3 12. Nxc7 {because of} Ng4
{and mate to follow. White now threatens 12 Bxh6 Bxh6 13 Nf6+.}) 11... Bxg2 12.
Kxg2 ({Not} 12. Bxh6 {because of the reply} Qh3 {winning.}) 12... f5 13. b4
Rae8 14. f3 Nd8 15. Be3 c6 16. Ndc3 a6 17. b5 axb5 18. cxb5 Nhf7 19. Qb3 Kh8
20. Na4 Bh6 21. Nb6 Qe7 22. Bxh6 Nxh6 23. a4 fxe4 24. dxe4 ({If} 24. fxe4 {then
} Ng4) 24... Ne6 25. bxc6 bxc6 26. Qe3 Nf7 27. a5 Qa7 28. Ra1 Rb8 {The chances
are balanced.} 29. Rfc1 c5 30. Qd3 Nd4 31. Nxd4 exd4 32. f4 {To stop Ne5.} Rfe8
33. Re1 ({If} 33. e5 dxe5 34. Rxc5 {then} Rxb6 {wins.}) 33... Re7 34. Qc4 Qb7
35. Qd5 Qa6 ({Not} 35... Qxd5 {because} 36. exd5 {wins for White.}) 36. e5 dxe5
37. fxe5 Rd8 38. Qxc5 $2 ({Correct is} 38. Qc6 {when} Qb7 {leads to
approximate equality.}) 38... Qb7+ {Now Black is master of this vital long
diagonal and the white king is naked and in mortal danger.} 39. Kg1 Ng5 40. Ra3
Rf7 {With no less a threat than 41...Nh3 mate.} 41. h4 Nf3+ 42. Rxf3 Qxf3 0-1

