1. d4 Nf6 2. f3 d5 3. e4 e6 4. Be3 dxe4 {This is the best way to accept the
gambit, though it does allow transposition to a sort of French by 4 e5.} 5. Nc3
(5. Nd2 {is slightly better.}) 5... Bb4 6. Bg5 exf3 7. Nxf3 c5 {Preventing
White's natural Bd3.} 8. Bb5+ Bd7 9. Qe2 Bxb5 10. Qxb5+ Qd7 11. O-O-O ({
Also possible but less forcing is} 11. Qe2 {intending 12.0-0-0; or if} Nd5 12.
O-O $1 Nxc3 13. bxc3 Bxc3 14. Rad1 {e.g.} Bxd4+ 15. Rxd4 cxd4 16. Ne5 Qc7 {
('QK2')} 17. Rxf7 Qxf7 18. Nxf7 Kxf7 19. Qf3+ {with some advantage.}) 11...
Bxc3 ({Of course not} 11... Qxb5 12. Nxb5 Na6 13. Nd6+ {winning back the pawn
with advantage.}) 12. Qxc5 $1 Ne4 ({There is much to be said for} 12... Qc6 {
though after} 13. Qa3 {White retains pressure.}) 13. Qe5 Bxb2+ ({If} 13... Nxg5
14. Qxg7 Rf8 15. Nxg5 Bb4 16. Nxh7) 14. Kxb2 Nf2 15. Qxg7 Nxd1+ 16. Rxd1 Rf8
17. Bh6 Qb5+ 18. Kc1 Nd7 19. Qxh7 Nf6 $2 ({Better} 19... Qh5 {though} 20. Rd3
$1 {, preventing} O-O-O {because of} 21. Rc3+ Kb8 22. Bf4+ {and 23 Qxh5, keeps
up the pressure.}) 20. Qg7 Nd7 21. d5 O-O-O 22. Qc3+ Kb8 23. dxe6 fxe6 ({Not} 
23... Nb6 24. Bxf8 Rxf8 25. e7) ({or} 23... Rc8 24. exd7 $1 Rxc3 25. Bf4+ {
and mates.}) 24. Bxf8 Rxf8 25. Qd4 Rd8 $2 ({A final blunder though after} 25...
Rf7 26. Qd6+ Kc8 27. Qxe6 {Black has little hope.}) 26. Ne5 Kc8 27. Nxd7 1-0

