1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bg5 {A new move from Taimanov.} Ne4 5. Bh4 Bg7
6. Nf3 c5 7. e3 cxd4 8. exd4 Nc6 9. cxd5 Nxc3 10. bxc3 Qxd5 11. Be2 O-O 12. O-O
{White stands slightly better. His pressure on the black e-pawn is somewhat
embarrassing.} Qd8 13. Re1 Re8 14. Qb3 {Hindering the development of Black's
c8-bishop and threatening to attack the f7 square.} Na5 15. Qa3 {Threatening
16 Bb5 winning outright - the move which Black prevents on his next turn.} Bd7
16. Bf1 f6 ({If} 16... Bf8 17. Ne5 Be6 18. Bb5 {wins the exchange.}) 17. Nd2
Rc8 18. Nb3 Nc6 19. Nc5 b6 20. Bc4+ Kh8 21. Ne6 $1 ({If} 21. Nxd7 {then not 21.
..Qxd7 because of 22 Be6 but rather} Nxd4 {with complications favouring White.
After the text Black is completely hamstrung. The queen hasn't even one square
to move to!}) 21... Bxe6 22. Bxe6 Ra8 ({If} 22... Rc7 {or 22...Rb8 white gains
a tempo with Bg3.}) 23. Bg3 Rf8 24. Rad1 {Threatening an eventual breakthrough
with d6.} f5 25. Bf4 Bf6 26. Qc1 Qe8 27. Bh6 Bg7 28. Rd3 Rf6 29. Rh3 Qf8 {
To meet the threat of 30 Bxg7+ Kxg7 31 Qh6+ Kh8 32 Qxh7 mate.} 30. Bg5 1-0

