1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qb3 c5 5. dxc5 Bxc5 ({More usual is} 5... Na6)
6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Bg5 Be7 8. e4 d6 9. Be2 Qc7 {At this point I noticed to my
horror that I was playing against a Maroczy Bind.} 10. O-O Bd7 11. Rac1 O-O 12.
Rfd1 a6 {This is regrettably necessary as 13 Bxf6 would otherwise have forced
13...gxf6.} 13. Be3 (13. Nd5 {is possible but it weakens White's hold on the
centre.}) 13... Rac8 14. Bb6 Qb8 15. Rd2 Ne5 $1 {This is Black’s only hope.}
16. Nxe5 dxe5 17. Rcd1 Bc6 18. f3 Rfe8 ({To prepare for 19...Bd8. If at once} 
18... Bd8 19. Bc5 Re8 20. Bd6 Bc7 21. c5 {which is overwhelming.}) 19. a4 Bd8
20. a5 Bc7 21. Na4 Bxa4 22. Qxa4 Red8 ({If} 22... Rcd8 23. Qb4 {and 24 Qc5 is
hard to answer.}) 23. Qb4 h6 24. Kf2 Rxd2 25. Rxd2 (25. Qxd2 {is also very
reasonable.} Bxb6+ {is then forced.}) 25... Rd8 26. c5 ({If} 26. Bxc7 Qxc7 27.
Rxd8+ Qxd8 28. Qxb7 Qd4+ 29. Kf1 Nd7 30. Qxa6 Nc5 {leaves it very difficult
for White to avoid a perpetual check. Possibly then correct was 24 g3.}) 26...
Rxd2 27. Qxd2 Kf8 $2 ({Much better was} 27... Qc8) 28. Qb4 Kg8 29. Ke1 Nd7 30.
Qc3 Qc8 31. Kd2 Bd8 32. b4 Be7 33. Kc2 Nb8 34. b5 ({If now} 34. Qxe5 Nc6 {
and Bf6 with considerable play on the black squares}) 34... axb5 35. Bxb5 Nc6
36. Qc4 Qd7 37. Bxc6 Qxc6 38. Kb3 Qd7 (38... Kf8 {is easier but quite frankly
Black was in too much time trouble.}) 39. c6 bxc6 40. a6 Qd1+ 41. Kb2 ({If} 41.
Qc2 Qa1 {draws.}) 41... Qd2+ 42. Kb1 Qd1+ 43. Ka2 Qd2+ 1/2-1/2

