1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. O-O d6 6. d4 Nbd7 7. Nc3 e5 8. e4
exd4 9. Nxd4 Re8 10. Be3 ({In Larsen-Stein, Belgrade '70 White played} 10. Re1
{- 10 Be3 may be an innovation. (It wasn't - JS)}) 10... Ne5 11. b3 Neg4 12.
Bf4 {Enticing Black's reply - an error.} Nh5 13. Bc1 ({Much better than} 13. h3
Nxf4 14. gxf4 Nf6 {because White becomes so weak on the black squares.}) 13...
c6 14. h3 Qb6 15. hxg4 Nxg3 ({If} 15... Bxd4 16. Na4 {wins}) ({or} 15... Qxd4
16. gxh5 Qxd1 17. Rxd1 Bxc3 18. Rb1 {and White has a greatly superior position
due to the weakness of Black's d-pawn.}) 16. Be3 Nxf1 17. Kxf1 c5 ({If} 17...
Bxg4 $2 18. Qxg4 Bxd4 19. Na4 {as before.}) 18. Nd5 $1 Qd8 19. Nb5 Bxg4 20.
Qxg4 (20. f3 {is inferior as} Bh5 21. Nbc7 Rxe4 $1) 20... Bxa1 21. Nbc7 h5 $2 {
A blunder though Black is of course lost anyway.} 22. Qd1 Bg7 23. Nxe8 1-0

