1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. Nf3 Bg7 8. Be2
O-O 9. O-O Re8 10. Nd2 Na6 11. f3 Nc7 12. a4 b6 13. Kh1 Rb8 14. Nc4 Ba6 15. Ne3
$2 ({All White's problems stem from this move. It surrenders the initiative
and badly restricts the c1 bishop.} 15. Bg5 {was better.}) 15... Bxe2 {In
similar lines, Black normally does not wish to exchange his light-squared
bishop. Here, the Q-side play gained makes it worthwhile.} 16. Qxe2 a6 17. Qf2
b5 18. axb5 axb5 19. Bd2 Nd7 {Preparing to use e5 as a jumping-off point for
richer pastures.} 20. Ra2 Ne5 21. Ncd1 {It would have been better to have
attempted to double rooks on the a-file before playing this manoeuvre.} b4 22.
f4 $2 ({This loses a pawn. Better was} 22. Qe2 {or b3.}) 22... Nd3 23. Qe2 b3
24. Ra1 Nxb2 25. Nxb2 Bxb2 26. Rab1 Bg7 ({More accurate was} 26... Bd4) 27. Qd3
Qe7 28. Ba5 Na8 29. Rxb3 Rxb3 30. Qxb3 Qxe4 31. Nc4 {An error in time-trouble
but White is losing anyway.} Qxd5 32. Rd1 Bd4 33. Qb5 Re2 {Source: bulletin}
0-1

