1. e4 d6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nc3 c5 5. d3 Nc6 6. Nh3 Nf6 7. O-O Rb8 8. f4
Bg4 {A double-edged move which tempts early kingside expansion by White which
could be dangerous for Black.} 9. Qd2 Qc8 ({This could only be worthwhile if
Bh3 were possible.} 9... O-O {was better.}) 10. Nf2 Bd7 11. h3 h5 ({Consistent
but poor. This attempt to restrain the white kingside attack and to create
counterplay has a high price. It makes castling very difficult and renders
Black all the more vulnerable to central advances, in particular f5.} 11... O-O
{was still best.}) 12. Ncd1 b5 13. c3 e5 {A forced further weakening of
Black's pawn structure due to the threat of d4.} 14. Qe2 b4 15. Ne3 bxc3 16.
bxc3 Na5 {This strategy of intending to transfer the bishop to c6 or b5 is
much too slow. The knight itself soon becomes a target.} 17. f5 gxf5 18. Nxf5
Bxf5 19. exf5 Qxf5 {Not entirely satisfactory, but 20 g4 was hard to answer.}
20. Ne4 Qe6 21. Ng5 Qe7 22. d4 exd4 {Even if Black has to capture this is the
wrong way.} 23. Qa6 Qc7 24. Bf4 Qb6 25. Rae1+ Kd7 26. Qd3 Rhe8 27. Qf5+ Kc7 28.
Rb1 Qxb1 ({If} 28... Qa6 29. Nxf7 {wins.}) 29. Rxb1 Rxb1+ 30. Qxb1 Rb8 31.
Bxd6+ {Source: bulletin} 1-0

